> pickerInput("test_picker2", "Test picker:", choices = LETTERS[1:5])
> ```
> 
> Reload and see:
> 
> - If `selectInput` opens and `pickerInput` doesn’t, it’s almost certainly a conflicting JS/CSS or dependency order issue.
> - If *neither* opens, then something is intercepting clicks (overlay, modal, etc.).
> 
> ---
> 
> ### 2.3 Look for an overlay blocking clicks
> 
> In dev tools:
> 
> 1. Right-click on the picker → Inspect.
> 2. Move the mouse around on the page while watching which elements highlight.
> 3. If you see a large `<div>` that covers much of the page with high `z-index`, check its CSS in the Styles panel.
> 
> Typical culprits:
> 
> - A loading overlay from `waiter`, `shinybusy`, `shinycssloaders`, or your own CSS.
> - A modal backdrop that never got removed.
> 
