>     fluidPage(
>       # ... your existing Climate Risks UI ...
>     )
>   ),
> 
>   tabPanel(
>     "Adaptation Costs & Benefits",
>     fluidPage(
>       # ... your existing Adaptation UI ...
>     )
>   )
> )
> ```
> 
> If you switch to `navbarPage()` like this, you’ll be back on the standard Shiny Bootstrap 3 stack, and pickerInput should start opening again (just as in `picker_test.R`).
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Option 2 – Keep `page_navbar` but explicitly use Bootstrap 3
